Why Is Demand Increasing
AI and HPC Expansion: Growing demand for AI processors, data-center infrastructure, and high-performance computing is increasing the need for advanced packaging materials that support high computing density and thermal management.
Miniaturized Electronics: Smartphones, wearables, IoT devices, and other compact electronic products require packaging materials that enable smaller form factors while maintaining electrical and mechanical performance.
Advanced Packaging Adoption: Fan-out wafer-level packaging, 2.5D/3D packaging, system-in-package architectures, and chiplet integration are creating new requirements for substrates, underfills, die attach materials, and thermal solutions.

Semiconductor Packaging Watch: Chiplets and 3D Integration
Advanced packaging is becoming increasingly important as conventional semiconductor scaling faces greater technical and economic challenges. Materials supporting chiplet architectures, heterogeneous integration, high-bandwidth memory, and advanced thermal management are gaining importance as manufacturers seek higher performance and greater integration within compact packages.

